FILE: src/vUX-core-4.0.0-beta.js
FEATURE: border-color-cycle
DATE: 2026-10-11
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'core-fixes' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
$$.sm(el).animate() takes start = performance.now() when called, then measures each frame from
the requestAnimationFrame timestamp. The first frame's timestamp is the frame's start time and
can be earlier than that call, so timeFrac was negative and the first value drawn was below the
start value (and stored as the element's remembered value). Found when vilshub.com used
animate() to tween a colour index: the negative value indexed position -1, the draw function
threw, and that run died. Clamped to 0, as it was already clamped to 1 at the other end. CRLF kept.

OLD_SECTION
                    var timeFrac = (time - start) / options.duration;
                    if (timeFrac > 1) timeFrac = 1;

NEW_SECTION
                    var timeFrac = (time - start) / options.duration;
                    if (timeFrac > 1) timeFrac = 1;
                    //the first frame's timestamp can be earlier than performance.now() taken above, which
                    //made the first value fall below the start value
                    if (timeFrac < 0) timeFrac = 0;
